From cb94ac650ef1262c1514428efabf5198c9159032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: himax-hx8279: do not trust the page cache after a
 handoff

hx8279_set_page() keeps the last selected page and skips the B0 write
when the wanted page is already selected. On the bootloader handoff path
the panel is left exactly as the bootloader had it, including its page
pointer, while the cache still holds the zero it was initialised with.
The first set_page(0) after that therefore writes nothing and whatever
command follows is executed on the bootloader's page.

Until now nothing was sent on that path, so it never showed. The
previous patch sends the display on register there, and on the first
boot after it the panel came up at a very low brightness with the slider
at maximum: page 0 register B3 written while the DriverIC was still on
page 4, which is the backlight page. The first screen off switches to
the cold path, where the cache is correct again, and the brightness
returns to normal - which is exactly how it behaved.

Mark the page as unknown when taking over from the bootloader, so the
next set_page() always emits the B0 write.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
index bd2d56ee5b..3bb3bdd53a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx8279.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 
 /* Page selection */
 #define HX8279_REG_PAGE			0xb0
+ #define HX8279_PAGE_UNKNOWN			0xff
  #define HX8279_PAGE_SEL		GENMASK(3, 0)
 
 /* Identification */
@@ -1158,6 +1159,15 @@ static int hx8279_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
+		/*
+		 * The DriverIC is on whatever page the bootloader left it,
+		 * so the cache cannot be trusted: without this the first
+		 * hx8279_set_page() call sees the page it wants already
+		 * selected, writes nothing, and the command that follows
+		 * lands on the wrong page.
+		 */
+		hx->last_page = HX8279_PAGE_UNKNOWN;
+
 		hx->handoff = false;
 
 		/*
-- 
